
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5224

### ==============================
### USERS
### ==============================

### 1. Get All Users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### 2. Get User By ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create User
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{

  "name": "Dimas",
  "email": "dimas1@gmail.com",
  "phone": "081234567890"
}

### 4. Update User
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Andi",
  "email": "andid@gmail.com",
  "phone": "081234567891"
}


### ==============================
### WALLETS
### ==============================


### 5. Get Wallet By User ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/wallets/10
Accept: application/json

### 6. Top Up Wallet
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/wallets/10/topups
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 1000000,
  "description": "Top up via HTTP request"
}

### 7. Top Up - Invalid Amount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/wallets/1/topups
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 0,
  "description": "Invalid top up"
}


### ==============================
### TRANSACTIONS
### ==============================

### 8. Transfer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderUserId": 1,
  "receiverUserId": 2,
  "amount": 50000,
  "description": "Transfer to Budi"
}

### 9. Transfer - Insufficient Balance
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderUserId": 1,
  "receiverUserId": 2,
  "amount": 999999999,
  "description": "Insufficient balance test"
}

### 10. Transfer - Invalid Amount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderUserId": 1,
  "receiverUserId": 2,
  "amount": -10000,
  "description": "Invalid amount test"
}

### 11. Get User Transaction History
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/transactions
Accept: application/json
